\pard \fs24
{\plain \fs40 \i\f3\fs40 Concerning the Service}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 Christian marriage is a solemn and public covenant between a man and a\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 woman in the presence of God.  In the Episcopal Church it is required that \par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 one, at least, of the parties must be a baptized Christian; that the \par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 ceremony be attested by at least two witnesses; and that the marriage \par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 conform to the laws of the State and the canons of this Church.\par
}\pard \fs20\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20  \par
}\pard \fs20
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 A priest or a bishop normally presides at the Celebration and Blessing\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 of a Marriage, because such ministers alone have the function of \par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 pronouncing the nuptial blessing, and of celebrating the Holy Eucharist.\par
}\pard \fs20\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 \par
}\pard \fs20
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 When both a bishop and a priest are present and officiating, the bishop\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 should pronounce the blessing and preside at the Eucharist.\par
}\pard \fs20\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 \par
}\pard \fs20
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 A deacon, or an assisting priest, may deliver the charge, ask for the\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 Declaration of Consent, read the Gospel, and perform other assisting \par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 functions at the Eucharist.\par
}\pard \fs20\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 \par
}\pard \fs20
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 Where it is permitted by civil law that deacons may perform marriages,\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 and no priest or bishop is available, a deacon may use the service which\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 follows, omitting the nuptial blessing which follows The Prayers.\par
}\pard \fs20\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20  \par
}\pard \fs20
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 It is desirable that the Lessons from the Old Testament and the Epistles be \par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 read by lay persons.\par
}\pard \fs20\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20  \par
}\pard \fs20
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 In the opening exhortation (at the symbol of }{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 N.N}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 .), the full names of the \par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 persons to be married are declared.  Subsequently, only their Christian \par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 names are used.\par
}\pard \fs20\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20  \par
}\pard \fs20
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 Additional Directions are on page 437.\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20  \par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 \par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 \par
}\column 
\pard \fs48
{\plain \fs48 \b\f3\fs48 The Celebration and\par
}\pard \fs48\sl72\slmult1 
{\plain \fs48 \b\f3\fs48 \par
}\pard \fs44
{\plain \fs48 \b\f3\fs48 Blessing of a Marriage}{\plain \fs44 \f3\fs44 \par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20  \par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 \par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 \par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 \par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 \par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 \par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 At the time appointed, the persons to be married, with their witnesses,\par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 assemble in the church or some other appropriate place.}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 \par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20  \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 During their entrance, a hymn, psalm, or anthem may be sung, or\par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 instrumental music may be played.}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 \par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20  \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 Then the Celebrant, facing the people and the persons to be married,\par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 with the woman to the right and the man to the left, addresses the\par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 congregation and says}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 \par
}\pard \fs20\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20  \par
}\pard \fs24
{\plain \fs24 \f3 Dearly beloved: We have come together in the presence of\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 God to witness and bless the joining together of this man and\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 this woman in Holy Matrimony.  The bond and covenant of\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 marriage was established by God in creation, and our Lord\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 Jesus Christ adorned this manner of life by his presence and\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 first miracle at a wedding in Cana of Galilee.  It signifies to us\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 the mystery of the union between Christ and his Church, and\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 Holy Scripture commends it to be honored among all people.\par
}\pard \fs24\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}\pard \fs24
{\plain \fs24 \f3 The union of husband and wife in heart, body, and mind is\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 intended by God for their mutual joy; for the help and comfort\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 given one another in prosperity and adversity; and, when it is\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 God{\u8217\'92}s will, for the procreation of children and their nurture\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 in the knowledge and love of the Lord.  Therefore marriage is\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 not to be entered into unadvisedly or lightly, but reverently,\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 deliberately, and in accordance with the purposes for which it\par
}\pard \fs24\tx-720\tx0\tx612\tx1152\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8532\tx9072\tx10080\tx10800\tx11520\tx12240\tx12960\tx13680\tx14400\tx15120\tx15840\tx16560\tx17280\tx18000\tx18720
{\plain \fs24 \f3 was instituted by God. \par
}\column 
\pard \fs24\tx-720\tx0\tx612\tx1152\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8532\tx9072\tx10080\tx10800\tx11520\tx12240\tx12960\tx13680\tx14400\tx15120\tx15840\tx16560\tx17280\tx18000\tx18720
{\plain \fs24 \f3 Into this holy union }{\plain \fs24 \i\f3 N.N}{\plain \fs24 \f3 . and }{\plain \fs24 \i\f3 N.N.}{\plain \fs24 \f3  now come to be joined.  \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 If any of you can show just cause why they may not lawfully be\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 married, speak now; or else for ever hold your peace.\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 Then the Celebrant says to the persons to be married}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}\pard \fs24\sl120\slmult1\tx-720\tx0\tx612\tx1152\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8532\tx9072\tx10080\tx10800\tx11520\tx12240\tx12960\tx13680\tx14400\tx15120\tx15840\tx16560\tx17280\tx18000\tx18720 
{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}\pard \fs24\tx-720\tx0\tx612\tx1152\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8532\tx9072\tx10080\tx10800\tx11520\tx12240\tx12960\tx13680\tx14400\tx15120\tx15840\tx16560\tx17280\tx18000\tx18720
{\plain \fs24 \f3 I require and charge you both, here in the presence of God,\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 that if either of you know any reason why you may not be\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 united in marriage lawfully, and in accordance with God{\u8217\'92}s\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 Word, you do now confess it.\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}{\plain \fs24 \b\f3 The Declaration of Consent}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 The Celebrant says to the woman}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}\pard \fs24\sl120\slmult1\tx-720\tx0\tx612\tx1152\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8532\tx9072\tx10080\tx10800\tx11520\tx12240\tx12960\tx13680\tx14400\tx15120\tx15840\tx16560\tx17280\tx18000\tx18720 
{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}\pard \fs24\tx-720\tx0\tx612\tx1152\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8532\tx9072\tx10080\tx10800\tx11520\tx12240\tx12960\tx13680\tx14400\tx15120\tx15840\tx16560\tx17280\tx18000\tx18720
{\plain \fs24 \i\f3 N}{\plain \fs24 \f3 ., will you have this man to be your husband; to live\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 together in the covenant of marriage?  Will you love him,\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 comfort him, honor and keep him, in sickness and in health;\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 and, forsaking all others, be faithful to him as long as you\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 both shall live?\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 The Woman answers}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}\pard \fs24\sl120\slmult1\tx-720\tx0\tx612\tx1152\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8532\tx9072\tx10080\tx10800\tx11520\tx12240\tx12960\tx13680\tx14400\tx15120\tx15840\tx16560\tx17280\tx18000\tx18720 
{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}\pard \fs24\tx-720\tx0\tx612\tx1152\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8532\tx9072\tx10080\tx10800\tx11520\tx12240\tx12960\tx13680\tx14400\tx15120\tx15840\tx16560\tx17280\tx18000\tx18720
{\plain \fs24 \f3 I will.\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 The Celebrant says to the man}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}\pard \fs24\sl120\slmult1\tx-720\tx0\tx612\tx1152\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8532\tx9072\tx10080\tx10800\tx11520\tx12240\tx12960\tx13680\tx14400\tx15120\tx15840\tx16560\tx17280\tx18000\tx18720 
