{\plain \fs24 \b\f3 At the Eucharist}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 The liturgy continues with the Offertory, at which the newly married \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 couple may present the offerings of bread and wine}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 .}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}{\plain \fs24 \i\f3 Preface of Marriage}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 At the Communion, it is appropriate that the newly married couple\par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 receive Communion first, after the ministers}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 .}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 In place of the usual postcommunion prayer, the following is said}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}\pard \fs24\sl120\slmult1\tx-720\tx0\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3222\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\tx9360\tx10080\tx10800\tx11520\tx12240\tx12960\tx13680\tx14400\tx15120\tx15840\tx16560\tx17280\tx18000\tx18720 
{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}\pard \fs24\tx-720\tx0\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3222\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\tx9360\tx10080\tx10800\tx11520\tx12240\tx12960\tx13680\tx14400\tx15120\tx15840\tx16560\tx17280\tx18000\tx18720
{\plain \fs24 \f3 O God, the giver of all that is true and lovely and gracious:\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 We give you thanks for binding us together in these holy\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 mysteries of the Body and Blood of your Son Jesus Christ.\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 Grant that by your Holy Spirit,}{\plain \fs24 \i\f3  N}{\plain \fs24 \f3 . and }{\plain \fs24 \i\f3 N.}{\plain \fs24 \f3 , now joined in Holy\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 Matrimony, may become one in heart and soul, live in fidelity\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 and peace, and obtain those eternal joys prepared for all who\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3 love you; for the sake of Jesus Christ our Lord. }{\plain \fs24 \i\f3 Amen.}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 As the wedding party leaves the church, a hymn, psalm, or anthem may be\par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f3\fs20 sung, or instrumental music may be played.}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
